Question 5
Similar to Question 2, compare the year of approximate date of birth within each ppn and across datasets. Select only one year of approximate date of birth based on the most frequently reported value.
As opposed to coding above, we can look across the rows to take the most commonly reported year of approximate date of birth. Where the year value is reported equally among the multiple years, we will set to NA.



Show R code
#Most commonly reported year of birth
merged_data &lt;- merged_data %&gt;%
  rowwise() %&gt;%
  mutate(
    most_year_bod = {
      yrs &lt;- na.omit(c_across(starts_with("year_bod_")))
      if (length(yrs) == 0) NA_integer_
      else {
        tab &lt;- table(yrs)
        if (sum(tab == max(tab)) &gt; 1) NA_integer_
        else as.integer(names(tab)[which.max(tab)])
      }
    }
  ) %&gt;%
  ungroup()
